I'm a little familiar with the elemental planes above the
dungeon.  Anything special I need to make sure I have?  Will a
pick-axe suffice for the earth elemental?  Will a leviatation
spell suffice for the air elemental?  My AC is -27 (nothing yet
from donating to a priest; all the AC is stuff I'm wearing).
Is that low enough to make it through the astral plane?  Any
special wands that are particularly useful to have?

Finally, is there anyway to protect myself from the Wizard
cursing my stuff?  One poster responded that magic protection
was a yes or no thing.  This seems unfair that there is nothing
one can do to protect yourself from cursing.  Magic protection
should be variable such as from 0 - 100% protected (the way the
monsters are) with say GDSM going from 50% at +0 to maybe 75%
at +3.  Adding a cloak of magic protection would similarly add
more protection, making it harder and harder to get close to
100%.  Perhaps, confused enchant armor scrolls would make an
armor item curse resistant after it is fire/rustproof.

The Wizard should also not be forever regenerating.  Make him
like trolls so that he never regenerates to full HP, but do it
slowly so that he does get easier to kill maybe after 10 - 15
times.  After awhile it is more of an annoyance and makes the
game tedious.  I would rather face newer and tougher monsters
than the same old ones over and over again.

Is there anyway to increase HPs beyond the pittance that potions
do?  Why don't spell of healing and extra healing behave like
the potions and raise HPs?  

